    <sectiondef kind="typedef">
      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="group__safe__data__core__apis_1ga3c770b1d01f6dc639227675746e109ce" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>int(*</type>
        <definition>typedef int(* safe_data_mutator_t) (void *payload, void *user)</definition>
        <argsstring>)(void *payload, void *user)</argsstring>
        <name>safe_data_mutator_t</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Mutator callback used by <ref refid="group__safe__data__core__apis_1ga22c753dd75eb10609dbc8cf9ad12a5f6" kindref="member">safe_data_update()</ref> / <ref refid="group__safe__data__container__apis_1ga8e7e35fe3c39ac028c21f85fb3b8c1cd" kindref="member">SAFE_UPDATE()</ref>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Invoked with the lock held and the payload already verified. Mutate <computeroutput>payload</computeroutput> in place. Return 0 to commit (the integrity tag is resealed) or a negative errno to abort (the payload is rolled back / left as-is and NOT resealed). A positive return value is a contract violation: it is clamped to -EINVAL, the transaction aborts, and the event is counted in the statistics.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the (verified) payload, cast to its real type. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>user</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Opaque user context forwarded from the call site. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>0 to commit, negative errno to abort the transaction. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
