        <briefdescription>
<para>Atomic read-modify-write: lock, verify, run <computeroutput>fn</computeroutput>, reseal on success. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This is the correct &quot;checkout&quot;: the lock is held for the entire transaction and the integrity tag is resealed automatically, so it can never go stale.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lock</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Container mutex, or NULL to skip locking. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Payload buffer, verified before and resealed after <computeroutput>fn</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>len</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Payload size in bytes (&gt; 0). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>crc</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Integrity tag storage (resealed on commit). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>shadow</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Redundant shadow buffer of <computeroutput>len</computeroutput> bytes, or NULL if disabled (without it an aborting mutator must not have modified the payload - there is no rollback buffer). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fn</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Mutator invoked with the lock held and the payload verified. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>user</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Opaque context forwarded to <computeroutput>fn</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>0 on success, the mutator&apos;s negative return value if it aborts (a positive mutator return is clamped to -EINVAL), -EILSEQ if the pre-check fails unrecoverably, -EINVAL on bad args, -ETIMEDOUT if the lock bound expired. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
