        <briefdescription>
<para>Reseal after an explicit external modification (advanced use). Lock, recompute the integrity tag, unlock. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>Re-tags the current memory contents with NO verification - this can seal corrupted data. Only available with CONFIG_SAFE_DATA_ALLOW_UNCHECKED_COMMIT (off at the Strict level).</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lock</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Container mutex, or NULL to skip locking. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Payload buffer whose current contents are sealed as-is. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>len</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Payload size in bytes (&gt; 0). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>crc</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Integrity tag storage (recomputed). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>shadow</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
