        <name>SAFE_DATA_RECOVERED</name>
        <initializer>(-EAGAIN)</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Return code for a fault that the redundant shadow copy covers. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>From <ref refid="group__safe__data__core__apis_1ga5a7ff94945a049416e8edc6f0d3f019a" kindref="member">safe_data_verify()</ref> (pure) it means the fault is <emphasis>recoverable</emphasis>: the payload was NOT modified. From <ref refid="group__safe__data__core__apis_1ga08da109c60349a5bd8f6fbe8af830704" kindref="member">safe_data_verify_repair()</ref> it means the payload has been repaired in place and is valid again once the tag is resealed. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
